fix-mail-proxy-review-gaps progress

- Slice 1 fixed controlled shutdown: active IMAP/SMTP proxy connections are tracked by `mailproxy.Proxy` and closed after `ShutdownTimeout`; focused mailproxy tests cover stuck active sessions.
- Slice 2 fixed SMTP upstream TLS verification: STARTTLS `ServerName` now comes from the configured SMTP upstream host, with default Gmail behavior preserved.
- Slice 3 added the existing-service mail proxy toggle CLI: `vault service mail-proxy set <service>` mutates only `mail_proxy` fields on an exact service-name match and preserves unrelated service fields.
- Slice 4 cleaned the Hermes mail proxy patch whitespace and documented the new CLI toggle command in the Hermes Gmail guide.
- Archive prep removed non-normative `Previous` notes from MODIFIED deltas so OpenSpec can merge them into the living mail-proxy spec.
- OpenSpec archived `fix-mail-proxy-review-gaps` into `openspec/changes/archive/2026-07-01-fix-mail-proxy-review-gaps`.

fix-quota-account-identity progress

- Runtime quota state now keys multi-account counters, cooldowns, round-robin
  cursors, and usage output by `accounts[].id`.
- Credential lookup/injection still uses `accounts[].credential_key`, with
  selected account id propagated as non-secret request-log metadata.
- Request logs persist `account_id`; old rows still seed quota state from
  credential keys when account id is absent.
- Docs clarify account id vs credential key semantics.

add-credential-pool-eligibility progress

- Credentials now carry non-secret `pool_provider` metadata, defaulting to not
  poolable.
- Services with account pools now require `account_pool_provider`, and every
  account credential must match that provider.
- Credential/service UI and TypeScript SDK types expose the pool metadata.
- Docs and OpenSpec coverage updated for explicit pool opt-in.

add-account-only-rotation progress

- Account pools now activate runtime rotation without numeric quota caps.
- Empty quota policy applies no daily/monthly/rpm/concurrency limits, while
  cooldown and usage tracking still work per account id.
- Quota usage includes account-only services so the UI renders account states
  instead of generic configured text.
- Docs and coverage updated for account-only rotation.

fix-quota-ui-account-usage progress

- Account-only usage responses now include account rows, counters, state, and
  cooling availability without credential values.
- Services table receives account rows for account-only configs, avoiding the
  previous generic configured fallback.
- Coverage updated for API/UI usage visibility.

